  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 PM EDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nA rogue shower remains possible through sunset as one more weak\nwave passes through the area and interacts with limited \ninstability (less than 1000 J/KG MUCAPE) and little overall \nshear. \n\nOtherwise, an extended dry period is possible into next week with \nthe greatest confidence existing through this weekend on this \noccurring. The upper level flow will flatten somewhat and transition \nmore SW to NE into early next week then more west to east as a \nstrengthening upper level ridge pushes north. With the ridge axis \nremaining south of the region, this still leads to some uncertainty \nwith regards to weak waves that will pass through the flow. The flow \nwill reside far enough west into Sunday to keep precip chances west \nof the area with maybe some slightly better chances for a few \nshowers or storms during the work week. Forecast will remain riddled \nwith periods of slgt chc to chc pops especially next week as models \nstruggle to handle each of the waves. \n\nRegarding temperatures and humidity, seasonable highs in the lower \n80s and somewhat lower humidity settles in for Friday and Saturday. \nWarmer and more humid air begins to push back in with highs in the \nmid to upper 80s and dewpoints in the upper 60s to lower 70s Sunday \ninto next week.",
